  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nPeriods of rain with embedded thunder look to continue today\nbefore diminishing from west to east tonight as low pressure\nshifts away from the region. An additional 0.25\" to 0.50\" of\nrainfall accumulation are possible with the steadier showers\nbefore diminishing.\n\nPrecipitation chances will be more isolated over the weekend while\ntemperatures look to rebound. Highs by Sunday into Monday should\npush back into the 80s for much of NE Montana thanks to some\nridging extending over the area with the axis remaining to the\nwest.\n\nThat ridge looks to flatten by Monday night and Tuesday as the\nnext trough sets up over the Pacific Northwest. This will allow\nfor the next chance for steadier and more widespread rain showers\nto overtake the region.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nTemperatures were adjusted for Friday morning lows in coordination\nwith neighbors. Pops were also adjusted over the short term for\ncollaboration and consistency. Overall, NBM held the line through\nmuch of the forecast period. Confidence is high on cool and wet\nweather continuing for Friday with showers diminishing over the\nweekend.",
